== Background information ==
=== Title ===
* The title of this episode is a reference to the old English wedding rhyme "''Something old, something new, something borrowed, and something blue''", a [[superstition]] which encouraged a bride to incorporate these items into the ceremony in order to ensure a happy marriage.

=== Continuity ===
* Two classes of 22nd century Orion vessels that first appeared in {{s|ENT}}, namely the [[Orion Interceptor]] and [[Orion barge]], appear to still be in use during the 24th century.
* The mysterious small silver ship that appeared in {{e|Twovix}} and {{e|I Have No Bones Yet I Must Flee}} returns to destroy an Orion ship.
* This is the first appearance of the planet {{dis|Orion|planet}}, though a [[holodeck]] simulation of the [[Adashake Center]] on the planet was shown in {{LD|Second Contact}}.
* Mariner references [[Jonathan Archer]]'s encounter with [[Harrad-Sar's barge]] in {{ENT|Bound}}.
* A {{type|Raven}} [[Unnamed Raven type starships|starship]] was found in the [[ship graveyard]] on Orion.
* This is the first ''Star Trek'' series since {{s|TNG}} to include a [[Chalnoth]] character. The last one appeared in the [[TNG Season 3|Season 3]] episode {{e|Allegiance}}, which aired in 1990.
* The inscription on the Orion sedan chairs reads, in transliterated English, "This is a very fancy chair". This is in much the same vein as the alien inscription on the [[Krulmuth-B portal]] in {{SNW|Those Old Scientists}}, which Mariner and [[Nyota Uhura]] translated as "This is a time portal".

